{"name":"Light Blond","hex":"#e8d3af","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"blond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bleached or pale golden (light yellowish) colour.","Particularly of a person, having blond hair."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pale yellowish (golden brown) color, especially said of hair color.","A person with this hair color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blond","blocks":[{"text":"Blond or blonde, also referred to as fair hair, is a human hair color characterized by low levels of eumelanin, the dark pigment. The resultant visible hue depends on various factors, but always has some yellowish color. The color can be from the very pale blond to reddish \"strawberry\" blond or golden-brownish (\"sandy\") blond colors. Occasionally, the state of being blond, and specifically the occurrence of blond traits in a predominantly dark or colored population are referred to as blondism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/330px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blond","wikidata":"Q202466"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/1280px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of a portrait of Sigismund Casimir Vasa (c. 1644), with characteristic blond hair which darkened with time as confirmed by his later effigies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_(detail).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/500px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/1280px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/500px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_